WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.310
In 2022, for the first time, aquaculture
overtook wild capture as the main producer

2
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.190
of aquatic animals.

3
00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:15.310
By 2024 it supplied 103 million
tonnes, 53 per cent of the total.

4
00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.330
Meanwhile the high seas,
61 per cent of the ocean,

5
00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:24.210
belong to no one, and just
1.45 per cent is protected.

6
00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:27.490
So if we now farm more fish than we catch,

7
00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.410
is overfishing solved?

8
00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.330
Are wild stocks safe?

9
00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:35.330
In this mission, you'll read the FAO's
evidence on how many fish stocks are

10
00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:37.390
sustainable, and where.

11
00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.270
Then you'll meet the
tragedy of the commons,

12
00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:44.070
and judge quotas, protected areas
and the High Seas Agreement.

13
00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:49.300
Your mission: evaluate whether farming
more fish than we catch solves overfishing.
